# Production logs

Landing, `web-generation-worker`, and `payment-bot` push logs to Loki. When the user asks what happened in production, why a generation failed, or to check service health, call the Loki MCP tools `loki_status` and `loki_query`. They are read-only.

LogQL examples:

- `{service="landing", env="prod"}`
- `{service="landing", env="prod"} | json | event="product_snapshot"`
- `{service="web-generation-worker", env="prod", level="error"}`
- `{service="payment-bot", env="prod"}`

Do not print `LOKI_BASIC_AUTH` or copy the password into the repo. If the Loki MCP is not connected, say to enable `loki` in Cursor Settings → MCP. The password lives only in gitignored `.cursor/loki.env`.
